  "enable": "Modbus slave mode is active whenever the SW1 address is 1 or higher; address 0 selects stand-alone mode. Closing input S2 in slave mode selects clone mode, which disables Modbus control.",
  "watchdog": "Optional via SW1: with no holding-register write for 120 s the unit is switched on with its current settings and local control is unlocked or left as is, depending on the switch.",
  "quirks": [
   "Readback temperatures above 32767 are negative: subtract 65536 then divide by 100.",
   "Repeated identical writes in Last Touch mode override the user's remote; use On Change (3) for cyclic writers."
  ],
  "setup": [
   "9600 baud, no parity, 1 stop bit by default.",
   "Address on SW1 (0..63; 0 = stand-alone).",
   "RS485 3-wire: DB(+), DA(-), GND, daisy-chained."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
